! C22-6578 PROBLEM 4.7, "TRANSPOSITION OF A 64 x 64 BIT MATRIX", printed
! pp.40-41 (PDF 41-42), Method 2, read in the ink at 300 dpi.
!
!   "Given a 64x64 matrix whose elements are bits stored consecutively
!   and row-wise starting at BMX64.  Create the transpose and store it in
!   the same area."
!   "Method 2.  Use logical connectives.  The matrix is partitioned into
!   8x8 submatrices or blocks and each is transposed separately."
!   Comments: "(a) ... The (I, J)-block of the transposed matrix is the
!   transpose of the (J, I)-block of the original matrix.  (b) XW1, XW2,
!   XW3, and XW4 are not destroyed in the program. ..."
!
! THE PRINTED STATEMENTS, BMX64T TO "LOC SYN,BMX64", ARE AS PRINTED
! with one punctuation mark supplied (1 below).  BMX64 is the deck's.
! Assembled by the host STRAP II (ASM=strap2).
!
! WHAT IS READ IN THE INK AND IS WRONG AS PRINTED, two things:
!
!  1. The second line is printed "LX,$2,XW2;SX,$2,XW22,SX,$2,XW222": a
!     comma where the semicolon between two statements belongs (the
!     first line, "LX,$1,XW1;SX,$1,XW11;SX,$1,XW111", has both).  STRAP II
!     refuses the card as printed ("message 40: EXTRA FIELDS").  The
!     semicolon is supplied, and the deck runs with it.
!
!  2. >>> "XW2 XW,LOC,7,XW222" GIVES $2 A COUNT OF 7, AND $2 IS STEPPED
!     EIGHT TIMES A BLOCK. <<<  Read clearly at 300 dpi; XW1 beside it
!     prints 8.  $2 walks the eight rows of the (J, I) block by
!     progressive indexing with refill, "(V+ICR)", eight times in OFDIA1
!     and eight more in OFDIA2, exactly as $1 walks the (I, J) block with
!     its count of 8.  With 7 the count reaches zero on the seventh row
!     and $2 is refilled to the block's first row (Reference Manual
!     printed p.21 and p.26: refill "if the count reached zero"), so the
!     eighth row connected is row 0 again and the stores into the column
!     block land a row out of step.  The page's statement is not met.
!     THE DECK RUNS AS PRINTED, and with 8 ("--corrected": the one card
!     replaced in a copy, tests/verify_problem_4_matrix.py CORRECTIONS),
!     which gives the transpose.
!
! WHAT THE PROGRAM DOES, by the Reference Manual (printed page = PDF - 3).
!   $1 walks the row block (I, J), $2 the column block (J, I), each
!   0.64 a row by "(V+ICR)" (printed p.21) and refilled from XW111/XW222
!   to the block's first row; $3 is the offset index, in half words (an
!   integer in V-ICR's 19-bit field counts half words, C28-6129 Section I
!   printed pp.8-9), so V-ICR,$3,1 is one offset and V-ICR,$3,8 eight; $4
!   counts blocks.
!   DIAG1: "C0111(BU,8,1)(V+ICR),0.64($1),7($3)" ORs row r of the
!   diagonal block into the cleared accumulator at offset 7-r, which
!   lays A[r][c] at right-half bit 8c+r (problem_4_6_method2.strap has
!   the derivation, CONNECT printed pp.75-76).  DIAG2 stores the right
!   half's bytes, offset 56-8k, to rows k.
!   OFDIA1 does the same for the row block into the right half and the
!   column block at offset 71-r into the left half; the column block's
!   operand reaches 7-r bits past the accumulator's left end, where only
!   high-order zeros fall: "the storage operand is combined with the
!   accumulator operand up to the left end ...; higher-order bits in the
!   storage operand are dropped" (partial field, printed p.76).  OFDIA2
!   stores the right half (the row block transposed) into the column
!   block and the left half into the row block: the exchange.
!   $4: XW4 count 8, CBZR counts one at each diagonal, CBR one per pair,
!   refilled from XW44 at zero; NEWROW takes one more off XW44 (C-I), so
!   row I does 7 - I pairs and the eighth diagonal branches to BEW.
!
! THE DATA: problem_4_7_method1.strap's 64 words (Python
! random.Random(4707)).  THE EXPECTED VALUES are worked by
! tests/verify_problem_4_matrix.py, not taken from the model: the
! corrected run against the statement (the transpose), and both runs
! against a trace of the printed statements by the rules above, which is
! asserted to give the transpose when the count is 8 before it is used
! for the count of 7.  Checked: all 64 rows, $1-$4, XW11, XW22, XW44,
! XW111, XW222, the accumulator, the guards and the halt PC.
!   As printed (count 7): 1500 of the 4096 bits differ from the
!   transpose, in every one of the 64 rows; $2, XW22 and XW222 end with
!   count 7, where the corrected run ends them with 8.  The halt, $1,
!   $3, $4 and the accumulator are the same in both.
!
! PASSED AGAINST THE MODEL AS IT STOOD, BOTH RUNS: as printed the model
! stores exactly the trace's 64 wrong words, and corrected the transpose
! (77 exact checks and the PC each).  The column-block connect at
! offset 71-r runs past the accumulator's left end 28 x 7 times without
! disturbing anything.
!
! INJECTION, DATA SIDE, OBSERVED 2026-11-16:
!   the first word of BMX64 (16)09C4D5B1949524CB -> (16)01C4D5B1949524CB
!   (A[0][4] turned off), by --sub on the copy that runs; the expected words
!   are worked from the deck as it stands.  PREDICTED: row 4's bit 0.
!   OBSERVED, corrected: FAIL row04 only, (16)7A1A56121855F9EA for
!   (16)FA1A56121855F9EA.  OBSERVED, as printed: FAIL row04 only,
!   (16)7A1A5A99CCAACC55 for (16)FA1A5A99CCAACC55 (the printed program
!   happens to leave A[0][4] where the transpose puts it).  Everything
!   else passes in both.

! --- printed pp.40-41, Method 2 ----------------------------------------
BMX64T  LX,$1,XW1;SX,$1,XW11;SX,$1,XW111   !'row block index
        LX,$2,XW2;SX,$2,XW22;SX,$2,XW222   !'column block index
!                printed: LX,$2,XW2;SX,$2,XW22,SX,$2,XW222
        LX,$3,XW3                          !'offset index
        LX,$4,XW4;SX,$4,XW44               !'block counter
DIAG    LI(BU,1),0                      !'clear accumulator
DIAG1   C0111(BU,8,1)(V+ICR),0.64($1),7($3)     !'loop for diagonal block
        V-ICR,$3,1                      !'lower offset by 1
        BZXCZ,DIAG1                     !'until block completed
DIAG2   ST(BU,8,8)(V+ICR),0.64($1),64-8($3)     !'store diagonal block row-wise
        V-ICR,$3,8
        BZXCZ,DIAG2                     !'until block stored
        CBZR,$4,BEW                     !'branch if last diagonal block complete
OFDIAG  V+,$1,VFP8;SX,$1,XW111          !'loop for off diagonal block pair
        V+,$2,VF8P;SX,$2,XW222
        LI(BU,1),0
OFDIA1  C0111(BU,8,1)(V+ICR),0.64($1),7($3)     !'row block treatment
        C0111(BU,8,1)(V+ICR),0.64($2),64+7($3)  !'column block treatment
        V-ICR,$3,1                      !'lower offset
        BZXCZ,OFDIA1                    !'until block pair complete
OFDIA2  ST(BU,8,8)(V+ICR),0.64($2),64-8($3)     !'store into column block area
        ST(BU,8,8)(V+ICR),0.64($1),128-8($3)    !'store into row block area
        V-ICR,$3,8
        BZXCZ,OFDIA2                    !'until block pair stored
        CBR,$4,OFDIAG                   !'until one row, one column complete
NEWROW  LX,$1,XW11                      !'procedure for new row
        V+,$1,VF8P8
        SX,$1,XW11;SX,$1,XW111
        LX,$2,XW22
        V+, $2, VF8P8
        SX,$2,XW22;SX,$2,XW222
        C-I,$4,1;SX,$4,XW44
        B,DIAG
BEW     BEW,$
VFP8    VF,0.8
VF8P    VF,8.0
VF8P8   VF,8.8
XW1     XW,LOC,8,XW111
XW2     XW,LOC,7,XW222
XW3     XW,0,8,$
XW4     XW,0,8,XW44
XW11    XW,0                            !'to contain row information
XW22    XW,0                            !'to contain column information
XW44    XW,0                            !'to contain block counter
XW111   XW,0                            !'to contain row block information
XW222   XW,0                            !'to contain column block information
LOC     SYN,BMX64
! --- the deck's data ---------------------------------------------------
        SLC, 199.0
GUARD1  DD(BU,64),(16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
BMX64   DD(BU,64),(16)09C4D5B1949524CB
        DD(BU,64),(16)3E7CC7063D99F6DC
        DD(BU,64),(16)3C94FE7009B7D6BC
